# Briefcut settings for running from this checkout.
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# Then put your own key after MODEL_API_KEY= in .env.local.
# .env.local is listed in .gitignore, so it is never committed. This file is
# tracked and must never hold a real key.
#
# `bash scripts/studio.sh` and `uv run briefcut` (with no arguments) read
# .env.local. A variable already set in your shell wins over this file.
# You can also skip this file and paste the key in Studio under Settings.
#
# Keep each comment on its own line. Text after a value counts as part of it.

# Your Meta Model API key. Create one at https://dev.meta.ai
# Briefcut sends it only to api.meta.ai.
MODEL_API_KEY=

# 1 allows Meta calls. Briefcut makes no Meta call until this is 1 (or
# "Allow Meta calls" is on in Settings) and you start a project.
# <!-- VERIFY: does Meta-only mode keep this switch, or is it on whenever a key is set? -->
VEDIT_META_ENABLED=1

# standard or contributor.
#   standard     Muse Spark at the standard price ($1.25 in / $4.25 out per million tokens).
#   contributor  Muse Spark as muse-spark-1.3-contributor, at $0.10 / $0.20 per million
#                tokens. In exchange, Meta may train its future models on what you send
#                to Muse Spark: footage proxies, transcripts, briefs, notes, and caption
#                text. SAM 3.1, Muse Image, and Voice Transcribe have no contributor
#                variant and keep their normal prices and terms.
# Leave it on standard for client footage or for people who have not agreed.
VEDIT_META_MODE=standard

# The optional lines below are read only by scripts/studio.sh, which loads the
# whole file. `uv run briefcut` reads just the three settings above.

# Optional. Reasoning effort for Muse Spark: low, medium, or high. Default medium.
# VEDIT_META_REASONING=medium

# Optional. The FFmpeg to use. On a Mac, Homebrew's ffmpeg-full has the filters
# Briefcut needs (drawtext, subtitles). scripts/studio.sh picks it up when it is
# installed, so most people leave this unset.
# VEDIT_FFMPEG=/opt/homebrew/opt/ffmpeg-full/bin/ffmpeg
